    {
      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "178a922556bedde40c5fe77133099473",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"electron-pauli-form-factor-across-threshold\">Electron Pauli form factor across threshold</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><a href=\"/\">Browse all notebooks</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"/?file=hep/gminus2.py\">Generated vertex and g\u22122</a> \u00b7\n<a href=\"/?file=hep/ibp_differential_equations.py\">IBP differential equations</a> \u00b7\n<a href=\"/?file=hep/ibp_triangle.py\">Massless triangle</a></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The <a href=\"https://feyncalc.github.io/FeynCalcExamples/QED/OneLoop/El-GaEl\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">FeynCalc reference</a>\ncomputes <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(F_2(0)=\\alpha/(2\\pi)||)</marimo-tex>. Here we continue the same generated\nvertex to nonzero momentum transfer, including the physical timelike sheet.\nThe tree normalization, spin projectors, Dirac algebra and native IBP\nreduction come from the g\u22122 notebook through Marimo composition.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Write <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(r=t/m^2||)</marimo-tex> and <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(R(r)=F_2(t)/(\\alpha/(2\\pi))||)</marimo-tex>. Spacelike scattering\nhas <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(r&lt;0||)</marimo-tex>. Timelike values continue the crossed electron-pair current;\nits pair-production cut opens at <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(r=4||)</marimo-tex>. We use <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(t+i0||)</marimo-tex>, so the imaginary\npart is positive. Exactly at threshold the one-loop form factor diverges.\nThis notebook evaluates the Pauli form factor; it does not compute the\nrenormalized Dirac form factor <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(F_1||)</marimo-tex>.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
